.TH FORGE 1 "2026" "forge 0.1.0" "Forge Manual"
.SH NAME
forge \- a terminal text editor in the classic keyboard-driven tradition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forge
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forge is a modal-capable terminal editor: keys run named commands, help is built from the same structured documentation that this page is, and the manual can be read in the editor with \fIC\-h i\fR. Files named on the command line are visited in order; \fB+LINE[:COLUMN]\fR may precede a file name to move point into it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-file \fIFILE\fR
visit FILE (same as a positional file name)
.TP
.B \-\-find-file \fIFILE\fR
visit FILE (same as a positional file name)
.TP
.B \-\-visit \fIFILE\fR
visit FILE (same as a positional file name)
.TP
.B +LINE[:COLUMN]
go to LINE (and optional zero-based COLUMN) in the next file
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-load \fIFILE\fR
run FILE as a Rhai script
.TP
.B \-\-eval, \-\-execute \fIEXPR\fR
evaluate the Rhai expression EXPR
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-funcall \fICMD\fR
run the command CMD
.TP
.B \-\-insert \fIFILE\fR
insert the contents of FILE at point
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-directory \fIDIR\fR
load the plugins (.wasm files) in DIR
.TP
.B \-\-plugin \fIFILE\fR
load a plugin (a .wasm component); may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-kill
exit after the actions
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-no-init-file, \-\-no-config
don't run init.rhai or read the saved session
.TP
.B \-Q, \-\-quick
same as \-q
.TP
.B \-\-init-directory \fIDIR\fR
use DIR as the config directory (init.rhai, themes, plugins, grants)
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-user \fIUSER\fR
use the config directory of USER's home
.TP
.B \-\-chdir \fIDIR\fR
change to DIR before opening files
.TP
.B \-\-batch, \-batch
run the actions without a screen and exit; messages go to standard error, and the exit status is 1 on an error
.TP
.B \-\-script \fIFILE\fR
the same as \-\-batch \-l FILE
.TP
.B \-\-daemon[=NAME], \-\-bg-daemon[=NAME], \-\-fg-daemon[=NAME]
start as an edit server, in the background (the first two) or in this process
.TP
.B \-\-check-plugin \fIFILE\fR
load a plugin without the editor, show what it set up, run its commands (answering questions with \-\-answer), open files, wait for events and its processes' output
.TP
.B \-\-headless
run the editor without a terminal and print the screen (for testing plugins end to end)
.TP
.B \-\-package-entry \fIFILE.wasm\fR
print a package index entry for a plugin (see docs/plugin-api.md, "Sharing plugins")
.TP
.B package declarations \fI[\-\-json]\fR
collect use_package declarations without starting the editor; closures are reported, not run
.TP
.B package doctor \fI[\-\-json]\fR
check declared and installed plugins without starting the editor; exit status is 1 on an error finding
.TP
.B package sync \fI[\-\-json] [\-\-allow-build] [\-\-allow-capabilities] [\-\-allow-grants]\fR
install exactly what init.rhai declares and forge-lock.toml pins, without prompting; exit status is 0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 on bad usage and 3 when an operation needs an approval flag or setting
.TP
.B package snapshot diff \fIBEFORE AFTER [\-\-json]\fR
compare saved package snapshots without starting the editor; emit JSON with \-\-json
.TP
.B package lockfile diff \fIBEFORE AFTER [\-\-json]\fR
compare two lockfiles without starting the editor; emit JSON with \-\-json
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show the help
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
show the version
.SH SEE ALSO
The Forge manual: press \fIC\-h i\fR in the editor, or open \fImanual.html\fR on the documentation site. The \fBforge\fR plugin API is documented in \fIplugin-api.md\fR.
